A||||6||skitime||One year Fiero anniversary for Skitime and Veronica V6 GT (long)||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||08-19-2001||11:32 AM||||I just wanted to let everyone know that Saturday was an anniversary of sorts. One year ago, I was thinking about getting a Fiero and by luck noticed that there was a Fiero show a few miles away the very next day.  Veronica and I went to the Fiero Dutch Classic show and we thought how cool the cars were.  Veronica was thinking of getting another car too and began thinking she wanted a Fiero too.  I saw my first t-top at the show and decided that I wanted a red 88 GT t-top.  Well we started reading all we could find about Fieros and luckily found Pennocks Fiero Forum.  We also started searching for our Fieros on the internet in earnest.  Veronica found hers first in the state of Delaware through Autotrader.com.  It was an white 88 GT in very nice shape.  It only took her a little more than two weeks to find her car. We went to a local all Pontiac show to see more Fieros and decided just for fun to enter her car. She took third in the stock Fiero class and she was hooked. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-007f_8.jpg"> <BR> <BR>Finding a red 88 t-top that I could afford, proved to be more difficult. I was searching everywhere in all the club lists and internet sites that listed Fieros.  Finally during Christmas vacation, I found a listing in the Michigan Fiero Club Classified ads of a red 88 GT t-top out in Indiana.  I called and talked with a guy named Chris Moore.  He seemed very knowledgeable about Fieros which made me feel good about buying a car sight unseen. (Now that I am friends with Chris the last statement is a major understatement) He told me he considered the car to be in rough condition and needed work. Well I took an overnight Greyhound trip to Indiana to pick up the car. I drove it home in a snow storm while stopping every hour to add transmission fluid.  Here is the car before I owned it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/T_Drivers_Side_View-1.JPG"> <BR>And here is the car the way it is today.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080039-2_8.jpg"> <P>Well, yesterday we went back to that same show one year later and entered our cars in the Fiero Dutch Classic.  Veronica received a second place plaque in a very large stock GT class. She now has a collection of five trophies. I received the a first place plaque for custom GTs. It the first time I ever received a first place and I have two other trophies.  <P>The most amazing part of the past year for us is the wonderful people that we have come to know through the Fieros. We had a Fiero BBQ at our house last month and had over 25 people come and over 20 Fieros here. We just got back from a trip through the Maritime Provinces and now have even more Fiero friends we meet along the way. We know have friends throughout the United States and Canada even Australia.  The Fieros are amazing cars in more than one way!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierobaby||08-19-2001||11:47 AM||||CONGRATS!! that car is amazing it looked good when you got it but looks AMAZING now! that is awesome! I love your car so much I wish mine could look like that||||reg||1
